Contract: `OpenStore(path string) (Store, error)` returns a nil Store when opening fails. Callers are allowed to write `if st != nil { st.Close() }` after receiving an error. The implementation is:

```go
type Store interface {
    Close() error
}

type fileStore struct {
    name string
}

func (s *fileStore) Close() error {
    return nil
}

func OpenStore(path string) (Store, error) {
    fs, err := openFileStore(path)
    if err != nil {
        var empty *fileStore
        return empty, err
    }
    return fs, nil
}
```

Does this meet the contract? If not, name the bug and give the minimal fix.
